WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:06.120
Organelles are the specialized parts of the cell that have unique jobs to perform.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.360
Let's start with the nucleus, the control center of the cell.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.080
The nucleus contains DNA, or genetic material.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:25.140
The nucleus also contains a nucleolus, which is a structure where ribosomes are made.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:36.220
Ribosomes may wonder freely within the cytoplasm, or attach to the endoplasmic reticulum, sometimes abbreviated as E.R.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:43.860
Proteins and other materials emerge from the endoplasmic reticulum in small vesicles

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.300
where the Golgi apparatus, sometimes called the Golgi body, receives them.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.420
The Mitochondrion is an organelle that is the power house for both animal and plant cells.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.140
During a process called cellular respiration

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:08.780
the Mitochondria make ATP molecules that provide the energy for all of the cell's activities.

